    "qualification": "reject both placement candidates",
    "conclusion": "Coordinated placement improves local setup without adding area, but the complete route regresses setup, creates four capacitance and four hold violations, and increases congestion. Keep the previous 34-buffer design as the physical starting point.",
    "next_hypothesis": "Test placement and routing as one timing/electrical feedback loop, including explicit clock/hold treatment after global routing. The new hold failure is on unmoved cells and is dominated by altered clock delivery; isolated data placement against old routes is not a sufficient discriminator.",
